{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves-nonroad",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the NONROAD domain CATALOGUE, reading the DEFAULT DATABASE. It declares the 22 default-database tables `nonroad/model.esm` reads and mounts that model; a document per RunSpec in `runspecs/nonroad/` mounts THIS and supplies the run's selections and its oracle.\n\nNINETEEN OF THE FIRST TWENTY-ONE ARE COPIED WHOLE into an execution database, measured against `nr-logging-county`'s: every row of `nremissionrate`, `nrsourceusetype`, `nrbaseyearequippopulation`, `nrstatesurrogate` and the rest is there in both, and the only differences are two population rows in the thirteenth digit and seven formulations whose NULL oxygenate volumes the execution copy had already swept to 0. The other two, `nrfuelsupply` and `regioncounty`, are narrowed there (7,880 of 94,560 rows and 2 of 407,233), and the model already joined both on the run's fuel region, fuel year and month group -- so unlike the onroad catalogue's `link`, no selection the snapshot was making had been left unsaid.\n\nIT DOES NOT LOAD ALONE, by design: it names no runspec, and `esm validate` on it reports the sources it does not declare. IT DECLARES THREE METAPARAMETERS, all relays: `n_equipmentPoint`, `n_outputCohort` and `n_outputPolProcess` are the model's, and a RunSpec document can bind only what the document it mounts declares (docs/esm-conventions.md §49.1).\n\n`float_columns` appear for two reasons only. Every SCC is utf8 in the database and decodes to an exact Float64 key; and `nrGrowthIndex.growthIndex` is int64 with 43 NULLs -- growth pattern 1169 in every year -- which an integer column refuses to ingest and a float column carries as the NaN the execution copy's empty text also became.\n\nThe twenty-second is `nrFuelType`, for its `defaultFormulationID`: MOVES gives a selected fuel type with no supply its default formulation at market share 1.0, and at a state's pseudo-region that is the whole of the supply."
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_nremissionrate": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/nrEmissionRate.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "SCC"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nremissionrate"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "emission-factors"
        ],
        "note": "nrEmissionRate, the national table: 55,471 rows, every one of which the execution-database copy held too -- MOVES copies it whole. The zero-hour exhaust factors and BSFC (polProcess 9901), hp-binned per (SCC, engTechID); the `.EMF` file.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_nrdeterioration": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./movesdb/nrDeterioration.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_nrdeterioration"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "emission-factors"
        ],
        "note": "nrDeterioration, 424 rows, copied whole: the (A, B, cap) of `emfclc.f`'s deterioration per (polProcessID, engTechID).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_zonemonthhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
